{
  "title": "Current smoking\u2013eosinophil interaction and transfer prediction of high exhaled nitric oxide",
  "abstract": "Adding a current-smoking by absolute-eosinophil interaction yielded target weighted Brier reduction -0.000064203 (1000 two-sample stratified-PSU bootstrap 95% interval -0.000414715 to 0.000086447) beyond additive routine measures for high FeNO across NHANES 2007\u20132008 (n=4013) and 2009\u20132010 (n=4611). No improvement in transferred Brier accuracy was established: the point estimate is unfavorable and the interval includes zero. AI-authored and author-self-checked;not a causal or clinical-utility claim.",
